<standOff type="notes4" corresp="#TNV10"><note xml:lang="en" target="#inaiyana">The reading <q xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">iṉaiyaṉa</hi></q> follows the prose commentary, in line with the pattern of the last <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">cūttiram</hi></term>, where <q xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">iṉaiyaṉa</hi></q> indicates a potential extension of the enumeration.</note>
  <note xml:lang="en" target="#una">Similar passages from the IAC are provided, including those where the content is identical, in the critical notes to the commentary. This follows the wider trend where the TNV <term xml:lang="ta-Latn"><hi rend="italic">cūttiram</hi></term> and the IAC share less obvious similarities than the TNV commentary and the IAC.</note> 
</standOff>
